@s linux

- Cliquism in Linux and the Windows Community
- job search "it takes 10 lines to make a folder"
- game dev indies asks about it
- Just because I believe linux is one of the best operating systems and *nix is the best type of OS, doesn't mean everyone should.
- There are use cases for macos and windows

- Use the "try debian option on my usb"

- The type of people who use linux are developers, server administrators and such, therefore a lot of devs look at linux and help fix it
- Free and Open Source is considered the standard. Almost everything I use I expect to be able to see the source code
- Installing almost always happens with the package manager, if not then from source
- Apps tend to be a lot smaller as they are well written (with a lot of eyes on the code)

--- install.txt +=
# search godot on google and download
# or go to https://godotengine.org/download/linux/
# wget https://downloads.godotengine.org/?version=4.7.2&flavor=stable&slug=linux.x86_64.zip&platform=linux.64

apt search grafx2
sudo apt install grafx2

# search lmms
# install lmms alpha version
# consider the github releases as well
---

# Why Game development on linux?
## Negatives of developing on linux
- Most people don't develop on linux, so therefore usually the tools you use will be different which aren't "industry standard"
- But AAA games aren't selling as well, and indie games are on the rise!

## Positives of developing on linux
- All the benefits of linux in general
- Unix as an IDE
- dwm or a tiling window manager
- Works well for any sort of development
- terminal as a first-class citizen

--- stage_directions.txt +=
- play around with grafx2, make the title screen or banner art
- play around with lmms, make a song
---

--- stage_directions.txt +=
- Talk about the limitations of grafx2 and why you are going now with aseprite
- Talk about the limitations of lmms and why you are going with reaper
- Talk about how you can make amazing games with the tools we have covered however my personal preference changes

- Ask if everyone is clear as we are going to get a bit more technican and hands on after this
